# netsurf: borders -- sub-pixel widths snap to 1px, colours keep their
# alpha, rounded boxes get their real borders
#
# claude.ai's cards are drawn with Tailwind's border-[0.5px] in the
# default border colour (10% black):
# - FIXTOINT turned the 0.5px width into 0, so the border vanished. A
#   non-zero width under one device pixel now snaps up to 1px (CSS Values
#   4; what browsers do). Table cells (table.c) are unchanged.
# - nscss_color_to_ns() drops alpha, so translucent borders drew solid.
#   The border colour's alpha now goes into the border plot styles'
#   opacity (the mechanism rgba backgrounds use), set per plot and reset
#   to opaque after, so a caller that sets none draws as before; a fully
#   transparent border colour draws nothing.
# - A box with a border-radius skipped the border painter: MacSurf drew a
#   one-colour stroke with the background instead, which never read the
#   border width, so every rounded element with a border style (all of
#   them under Tailwind's preflight "border: 0 solid") got a solid 1px
#   frame, and per-side colours and alpha were lost. Rounded boxes now go
#   through the border painter like any other (square corners; the Vita
#   draws square backgrounds too).
